== directions/C1-requirements-first-field.md MASTER FORMULA
18:MASTER FORMULA (the tilted explicit formula, the field's identity backbone): for a > 1/2 and any window w >= 0 with hat-w supported in [-log X, log X], Sigma_rho m_rho Integral P_{a-beta}(t-gamma) w(t) dt = Arch_a(w) - Sigma_{n <= X} Lambda(n) n^{-a} (cos-transform of w)(log n), where P_x(y) = x/(x^2+y^2). The left side prices every zero by the Poisson kernel of its signed depth; the right side is an EXPLICIT archimedean term minus a FINITE nonneg-coefficient exponential sum. Locality is cheap in this coordinate: t-resolution of width 1 needs only X ~ e^{2*pi} ~ 535.
